26
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:34,220
Big love to everybody who's been watching.

27
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:35,420
Not medical advice,

28
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,650
talk to your doctor.

29
00:00:36,670 --> 00:00:37,930
Quick biology.

30
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:40,490
Any smoke means heat plus tiny particles

31
00:00:40,510 --> 00:00:41,690
hitting your lungs.

32
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:42,970
That's Neutro's turf,

33
00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:44,090
my security guard,

34
00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:45,930
patrolling the airways in the Don Valley

35
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:46,760
of the body.

36
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:48,680
All that smoke wears him out.

37
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:50,970
Weed smoke and tobacco smoke aren't the

38
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:51,690
same.

39
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:53,210
A review in the Annals of the

40
00:00:53,230 --> 00:00:55,450
American Thoracic Society says regular

41
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:57,690
weed smoking is linked to bronchitis symptoms

42
00:00:57,710 --> 00:00:59,370
that ease after you stop,

43
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:01,640
with far lower lung risk than tobacco.

44
00:01:01,870 --> 00:01:03,450
But tobacco-leaf wraps,

45
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:04,760
like blunts and grabba?

46
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:06,240
That's tobacco.

47
00:01:06,270 --> 00:01:08,410
Research on blunts shows they deliver real

48
00:01:08,430 --> 00:01:09,210
nicotine,

49
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:10,730
even when the stuff inside is something

50
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:11,450
else.

51
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:12,810
So a lot of people end up

52
00:01:12,830 --> 00:01:15,010
hooked on nicotine without realizing.

53
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:16,530
And this isn't niche.

54
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:18,490
About one in four Canadians used cannabis

55
00:01:18,510 --> 00:01:19,090
last year,

56
00:01:19,110 --> 00:01:20,410
per Health Canada.

57
00:01:20,430 --> 00:01:21,610
Keep watching for the number at the

58
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:22,250
end:

59
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:24,200
how many years you can get back.

60
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:24,880
Okay,

61
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:25,830
the countdown.

62
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,200
Twenty minutes:

63
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:28,910
heart rate starts dropping.

64
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:30,160
Twelve hours:

65
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:31,880
carbon monoxide in your blood is back

66
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:32,600
to normal,

67
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:34,520
so more oxygen reaches your muscles and

68
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:35,190
brain.

69
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,240
Two weeks to three months:

70
00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:40,070
circulation and lung function start improving.

71
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:41,520
One to nine months:

72
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:43,430
coughing and breathlessness drop.

73
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:45,400
Then the cravings.

74
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:47,120
That's your nicotine receptors asking for

75
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:47,960
a refill.

76
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:49,080
Totally normal.

77
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,000
They come in waves,

78
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:51,910
and every wave passes.

79
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:54,100
The first days are the loud part.

80
00:01:54,170 --> 00:01:55,030
Irritable,

81
00:01:55,050 --> 00:01:55,990
restless,

82
00:01:56,010 --> 00:01:57,510
sleep gets weird.

83
00:01:57,530 --> 00:01:58,270
For weed,

84
00:01:58,290 --> 00:02:00,710
a review in Substance Abuse and Rehabilitation

85
00:02:00,730 --> 00:02:02,630
says regular users can get a real

86
00:02:02,650 --> 00:02:03,710
withdrawal.

87
00:02:03,730 --> 00:02:05,350
Mostly mood and sleep stuff,

88
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:06,470
light to moderate.

89
00:02:06,490 --> 00:02:08,310
Your brain's cannabinoid receptors start

90
00:02:08,330 --> 00:02:10,150
resetting within two days.

91
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:11,830
Not dangerous for most people,

92
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:12,820
just annoying.

93
00:02:12,970 --> 00:02:13,700
Water,

94
00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:14,500
movement,

95
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:15,700
your people.

96
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,700
Week four is where it flips.

97
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:19,540
Those cannabinoid receptors are back to

98
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:20,580
normal functioning,

99
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,940
per that same review.

100
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:23,300
Cravings fade.

101
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,570
Sleep comes back.

102
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:25,460
In the Lungs,

103
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:27,460
Neutro finally gets a break.

104
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,340
The cilia,

105
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,340
tiny sweepers,

106
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,460
start moving again,

107
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,420
so you might cough more at first.

108
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:33,380
That's cleanup,

109
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,500
not failure.

110
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:35,490
Keep going.

111
00:02:35,510 --> 00:02:36,530
By one year,

112
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:38,530
the extra heart disease risk from smoking

113
00:02:38,550 --> 00:02:40,010
is about half.

114
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:41,170
By fifteen years,

115
00:02:41,190 --> 00:02:43,530
it matches someone who never smoked.

116
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:45,410
Airways keep healing too.

117
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:47,490
One study of COPD patients found the

118
00:02:47,510 --> 00:02:49,970
airway lining looked better in ex-smokers,

119
00:02:49,990 --> 00:02:51,450
mostly after more than three and a

120
00:02:51,470 --> 00:02:52,850
half years of quitting.

121
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:53,970
Real healing,

122
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:55,650
just not overnight.

123
00:02:55,670 --> 00:02:57,330
Now the number I promised.

124
00:02:57,350 --> 00:02:59,250
A study from Toronto's Centre for Global

125
00:02:59,270 --> 00:03:00,170
Health Research,

126
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:01,970
in the New England Journal of Medicine,

127
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:03,890
found smokers lose about a decade of

128
00:03:03,910 --> 00:03:04,770
life.

129
00:03:04,790 --> 00:03:06,650
Quit at 25 TO 34,

130
00:03:06,670 --> 00:03:08,610
you get back about 10 years.

131
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:10,170
35 TO 44,

132
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,250
about 9.

133
00:03:11,270 --> 00:03:12,850
45 TO 54,

134
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:13,970
about 6.

135
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:15,130
Quit before 40,

136
00:03:15,150 --> 00:03:16,690
and you cut that extra risk by

137
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:18,290
about 90%.

138
00:03:18,310 --> 00:03:19,330
Never too late,

139
00:03:19,350 --> 00:03:21,200
but sooner hits different.

140
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:22,240
Real talk:

141
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:23,920
quitting isn't willpower,

142
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:24,910
it's setup.

143
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:26,160
Tip one:

144
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:27,350
get a squad.

145
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,520
A big Cochrane review of over 300

146
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:31,720
trials found counselling raises your odds

147
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:34,160
of quitting by about 44%.

148
00:03:34,180 --> 00:03:36,240
Call or text Smokers' Helpline,

149
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,720
it's free and open 24/7:

150
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:43,040
1-877-513-5333,

151
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:47,040
or text iQuit to 123456.

152
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,160
Tell your group chat,

153
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:49,070
your roommate.

154
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,360
Text-message support looks helpful too.

155
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:52,910
Don't solo this.

156
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:53,960
Tip two:

157
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,150
ask a pharmacist.

158
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:56,880
If tobacco's in the mix,

159
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:58,240
